ax module of the \n      definition. \n    --no-alpha-renaming\n      Do not alpha rename anonymous variables in output.\n      Default: false\n    --no-sort-collections\n      Do not sort collections before printing (for speed).\n      Default: false\n    --no-substitution-filtering\n      Do not remove conjuncts of anonymous variables from substitution in \n      output. \n      Default: false\n    --output <mode>, -o <mode>\n      How to display krun results. <mode> is either \n      [pretty|program|kast|binary|json|kore|none]. \n      Default: KAST\n      Possible Values: [PRETTY, PROGRAM, KAST, JSON, KORE, NONE]\n    --output-file <file>\n      Store output in the file instead of displaying it.\n    --output-flatten <KLabels>\n      (Assoc) KLabels to flatten into one list.\n      Default: []\n    --output-omit <KLabels>\n      KLabels to omit from the output.\n      Default: []\n    --output-tokast <KLabels>\n      KLabels to output as KAST tokens.\n      Default: []\n    --output-tokenize <KLabels>\n      KLabels to tokenize underneath (reducing output size).\n      Default: []\n    --sort <sort>, -s <sort>\n      The start sort for the default parser. The default is the sort of $PGM \n      from the configuration. A sort may also be specified with the \n      'KRUN_SORT' environment variable, in which case it is used if the option \n      is not specified on the command line.\n    --steps <steps>\n      Apply specified kompilation steps to the parsed term. Only for --input \n      rule. Use --steps help for a detailed description of available steps.\n      Default: [anonVars]\n    --temp-dir <path>\n      Put temp files in this location. Default is /tmp/.<tool>-xxx\n    --verbose, -v\n      Print verbose output messages\n      Default: false\n    --version\n      Print version information\n      Default: false\n    --warnings <level>, -w <level>\n      Warning level. Values: [all|normal|none]\n      Default: NORMAL\n      Possible Values: [ALL, NORMAL, NONE]